    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are an executive assistant. Write a short, clear daily brief for my morning email using the data below. Keep it concise, use headers, and skip anything empty.\n\nCALENDAR EVENTS:\n{{ $json.calendar_events.map(item => `- ${item.summary} ${item.details} ${item.start_iso} ${item.end_iso}`).join('\\n') }}\nUNREAD EMAILS:\n{{ $json.Gmails.map(item => `- ${item.Sender} ${item.Subject} ${item.Snippet}`).join('\\n') }}\nTOP NEWS:\n{{ $json.articles_mapped.map(\n a => `- ${a.title} ${a.content}`\n).join('\\n') }}\nWEATHER:\n{{ $json.Tempreture }}\n{{ $json.Humidity }}\n{{ $json.Feels_like }}\nPENDING TASKS:\n{{ $json.Tasks.map(item => `- ${item.Kind} ${item.Status} ${item.Title}`).join('\\n') }}\nStart the email with a short, warm personal greeting (e.g. \"Good morning Hakim!\" plus one friendly line about the day ahead), and end with a brief, encouraging sign-off wishing me a productive day. Keep both the greeting and sign-off to 1-2 sentences, in the same HTML format as the rest.\nFormat the output as clean HTML suitable for an email body. Use <h3> for section titles, <b> for bold text, and <ul><li> for lists. Do NOT use Markdown syntax like ** or #. Sections: 📅 Schedule, 📧 Important Emails, 🌤️ Weather, 📰 News, ✅ Tasks.",
        "batching": {}
      },
